
<% if current_user.admin? %>
<h3>Guide for Admins</h3>

<div class="panel-group" id="accordion1" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true">
  <div class="panel panel-default">
    <div class="panel-heading" role="tab" id="headingOne">
      <h4 class="panel-title">
        <a role="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseOne">
          How does the Admin get started?
        </a>
      </h4>
    </div>
    <div id="collapse1" class="panel-collapse collapse in" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingOne">
      <div class="panel-body">
        <ul>
          <li>Click on the link you receive in your mail from Finly as soon as your organisation gets registered with us.</li>
          <li>Once you reset your password, log into the system and invite employees into the organisation.</li>
          <li>Streamline the flow of expenses within the organisation by assigning the appropriate roles to each of the employees and configuring who each of the employees reports to.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="panel panel-default">
    <div class="panel-heading" role="tab" id="headingTwo">
      <h4 class="panel-title">
        <a class="collapsed" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseTwo">
          How do I load money into my Finly Account?
        </a>
      </h4>
    </div>
    <div id="collapse2" class="panel-collapse collapse" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingTwo">
      <div class="panel-body">
        <p>
          If your loading money for the first time please add “Jouska Tech Pvt. Ltd”  as abeneficiary in your company’s Current Account. Once we are setup as a beneficiary inyour current account follow the below steps:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Transfer the funds to Finly.</li>
          <li>Once the transfer is successful a NEFT reference id will be generated for Finly.</li>
          <li>Enter this NEFT id, Date and Amount into the load Amount screen and submit it.</li>
          <li>Your Finly account will be credited latest by the end of the next business day.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="panel panel-default">
    <div class="panel-heading" role="tab" id="headingThree">
      <h4 class="panel-title">
        <a class="collapsed" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
          How many cards can I assign to each employee?
        </a>
      </h4>
    </div>
    <div id="collapse3" class="panel-collapse collapse" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingThree">
      <div class="panel-body">
        Each employee can be assigned only 1 card at any given point.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel panel-default">
    <div class="panel-heading" role="tab" id="headingThree">
      <h4 class="panel-title">
        <a class="collapsed" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
          What is the difference between <strong>Finly Account</strong> and <strong>Finly Expense Card</strong>?
        </a>
      </h4>
    </div>
    <div id="collapse4" class="panel-collapse collapse" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingThree">
      <div class="panel-body">
        <p><strong>Finly Account</strong> has no fund limit and once a transfer is made to employee’s accountit can be withdrawn</p>
        <p><strong>Finly Expense Card</strong> has a holding limit of INR 50,000/- if the KYC is submitted or has aholding limit of INR 10,000/- for non-KYC cards. Also, once money is loaded into the card, it cannot be withdrawn.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel panel-default">
    <div class="panel-heading" role="tab" id="headingThree">
      <h4 class="panel-title">
        <a class="collapsed" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
          Can I make a transfer to the Employee Account or Employee Card anytime?
        </a>
      </h4>
    </div>
    <div id="collapse5" class="panel-collapse collapse" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingThree">
      <div class="panel-body">
        Yes. You can load the employee account/ card, anytime, instantly, 24/7, 365 days in a year.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<% end %>

<h3>Finly Expense Cards</h3>



<div class="panel-group" id="accordion2" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true">
  <div class="panel panel-default">
    <div class="panel-heading" role="tab" id="headingOne">
      <h4 class="panel-title">
        <a role="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse6" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseOne">
          What is the Finly Standard Card ?
        </a>
      </h4>
    </div>
    <div id="collapse6" class="panel-collapse collapse" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingOne">
      <div class="panel-body">
        <ul>
          <li>You do not need to submit your KYC documents to get your hands on these cards.</li>
          <li>No ATM withdrawal allowed on this card.</li>
          <li>Fund holding limit for FSC card is INR 10,000/-</li>
          <li>Monthly withdrawal limit of INR 10,000/-</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="panel panel-default">
    <div class="panel-heading" role="tab" id="headingTwo">
      <h4 class="panel-title">
        <a class="collapsed" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseTwo">
          What is the Finly Premium Card ?
        </a>
      </h4>
    </div>
    <div id="collapse7" class="panel-collapse collapse" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingTwo">
      <div class="panel-body">
        <ul>
          <li>You need to submit your KYC documents to gain access to more functionalities.</li>
          <li>Fund holding limit for FPC card is INR 50,000/-</li>
          <li>Can be used to withdraw money in ATMs.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="panel panel-default">
    <div class="panel-heading" role="tab" id="headingThree">
      <h4 class="panel-title">
        <a class="collapsed" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
          Are these Cards accepted anywhere?
        </a>
      </h4>
    </div>
    <div id="collapse8" class="panel-collapse collapse" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingThree">
      <div class="panel-body">
        Yes. These cards can be used in all places that accept VISA. You can also used thesecards to pay on web portals that allow online payments. Additionally, the FPC card can be used to withdraw money from the card at any ATM for a fixed charge of INR 25/- per withdrawal.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel panel-default">
    <div class="panel-heading" role="tab" id="headingThree">
      <h4 class="panel-title">
        <a class="collapsed" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse9" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
          How do I use this card at a POS terminal of offline merchants like grocery stores or movie theatres?
        </a>
      </h4>
    </div>
    <div id="collapse9" class="panel-collapse collapse" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingThree">
      <div class="panel-body">
        The cashier can swipe the card like any other card through the POS machine. You will be asked to enter the pin to authenticate the transaction.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel panel-default">
    <div class="panel-heading" role="tab" id="headingThree">
      <h4 class="panel-title">
        <a class="collapsed" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse10" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
          What if the Finly card is stolen?
        </a>
      </h4>
    </div>
    <div id="collapse10" class="panel-collapse collapse" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingThree">
      <div class="panel-body">
        You can turn off the card using Finly web portal or the mobile app. You don’t have to worry about calling Finly or the Bank. You have complete control to block/ unblock the card.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel panel-default">
    <div class="panel-heading" role="tab" id="headingThree">
      <h4 class="panel-title">
        <a class="collapsed" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse11" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
          What if we want to replace the card?
        </a>
      </h4>
    </div>
    <div id="collapse11" class="panel-collapse collapse" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingThree">
      <div class="panel-body">
        You will have to order a new card for the employee. Please drop a mail at help@finly.io, we would be happy to guide you through this process.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel panel-default">
    <div class="panel-heading" role="tab" id="headingThree">
      <h4 class="panel-title">
        <a class="collapsed" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse12" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
          What happens when employee leaves the company?
        </a>
      </h4>
    </div>
    <div id="collapse12" class="panel-collapse collapse" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingThree">
      <div class="panel-body">
        You can turn off the card using Finly web portal or the mobile app. Please drop a mail athelp@finly.io, we would be happy to guide you through deactivating the card.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h3>Security</h3>
<div class="panel-group" id="accordion3" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true">
  <div class="panel panel-default">
    <div class="panel-heading" role="tab" id="headingThree">
      <h4 class="panel-title">
        <a class="collapsed" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse13" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
          How secure is Finly?
        </a>
      </h4>
    </div>
    <div id="collapse13" class="panel-collapse collapse" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingThree">
      <div class="panel-body">
        <p>
          The funds that you have loaded onto Finly account is deposited with the either HDFC, RBL or Kotak bank as per the choice you would have made while signing up, and are protected under the banks security norms. Also, only the authorized company admin canlog into Finly’s dashboard and access these funds.  
        </p>
        <p>
          Our technology is PCI complied ensuring a secure environment for all information with respect to the prepaid card.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel panel-default">
    <div class="panel-heading" role="tab" id="headingThree">
      <h4 class="panel-title">
        <a class="collapsed" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="#collapse14" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
          Is Finly regulated by a government body?
        </a>
      </h4>
    </div>
    <div id="collapse14" class="panel-collapse collapse" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="headingThree">
      <div class="panel-body">
        Finly operates under the RBI guidelines and also falls under RBI supervision andregulation.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>